  "scope_and_limitations": [
    "Real loopback WebSocket/Tunnel/InstructionPump/Parser/Client/image decode/canvas draw and actual ordered sync ACKs execute. Preencoded payloads exclude capture and native planner/encoder speed; static asset encode_ms values are informational only.",
    "Pacing is an approximate 16 ms target with application-level bandwidth/release delay/seeded jitter. Loopback ACKs are unshaped; this does not emulate Wi-Fi loss, TCP congestion, actual RTT, physical input or display paint/FPS.",
    "Sender and browser clocks are separate, never subtracted across domains. Scheduled-source-due-to-ACK is a schedule/backlog proxy, not latency from actual capture or proof of immediate kernel delivery. Source timer early/late records remain complete.",
    "Transfer and decode overlap. Browser image-dispatch-to-sync includes arrival/parsing/handlers; sync-to-ACK includes remaining decode/frame wait/draw and audio synchronization. Intervals are not independent additive CPU stages.",
    "Every image frame has draw-coordinate/count/order and exactly-once sync-ACK checks. Exact RGBA is read per frame only in separate ACK-gated verification documents; timing runs check only final pixels. Readback counts are reported separately from all frame counts.",
    "PNG Image/data-URI references and WebP Image/RGB plus native complete-buffer references are checked exactly. Actual VideoFrame.format selects the WebP representation, never a tolerance or best pixel match. Native WebP reference is not an independent decoder algorithm and original lossy source RGB equality is not claimed.",
    "Optional Base64/copy instrumentation runs only after oracle construction in separate verification pages. The default comparison has null diagnostics snapshots everywhere; enabled correctness probes intentionally incur optional measurements.",
    "Display snapshots can miss partial/not-yet-arrived frames and transient spikes. A low browser display queue does not imply low update latency: source schedule debt reaches 3.833 seconds under the constrained profile.",
    "Summary p95 values are arithmetic means of four per-run nearest-rank p95s, not pooled percentiles. With 12 measured frames, each per-run p95 is that run's maximum. Short mixed results and historical A/A data do not establish a browser gain or universally exclude regressions."
  ],
